# Workflow Orchestrator

Two tracks share this repo. Read `docs/PROJECT_STATE.md` and act only on the active track.

New projects start at `STATUS: PENDING_RESEARCH_APPROVAL`. Run `@01-researcher` first.

## Build track (greenfield → first production)
1. `@01-researcher` → Gate 1 (Market & Idea)
2. `@02-architect` → Gate 2 (Architecture & Cost)
3. `@03-manager` → Gate 3 (Sprint Tickets)
4. `@04-dev-fullstack` → implement tickets
5. `@08-ui-artist` → screenshot visual pass (UI-touching tickets)
6. `@06-dev-qa` → verify tickets
7. `@05-dev-ops` → Gate 4 (Production Release)

## Maintenance track (feedback → hotfix/release)
1. `@01-researcher` and/or `@07-dev-maintenance` → Gate M1 (Feedback & Backlog)
2. `@02-architect` evaluates structural impact when refactors or complex features are proposed
3. `@03-manager` → Gate M2 (Maintenance Sprint)
4. `@04-dev-fullstack` and/or `@07-dev-maintenance` → implement tickets
5. `@08-ui-artist` → screenshot visual pass (UI-touching tickets)
6. `@06-dev-qa` → regression verify
7. `@05-dev-ops` stages release → Gate M3 (Hotfix & Release)

## Before every action
1. Read `docs/PROJECT_STATE.md`.
2. Act only as the role for the current phase / track. Do not skip gates.
3. Build track: do not write application code until Gate 3 is checked off.
4. Maintenance track: do not write application code until Gate M2 is checked off (except read-only triage by `@07-dev-maintenance`).
5. `@08-ui-artist` screenshot review is allowed any time; visual-only code still follows Gate 3 / M2.

## On user reply `APPROVED`
### Build track
1. Check off the gate matching the current build `STATUS`.
2. Update `STATUS`:
   - After Gate 1 → `PENDING_ARCHITECTURE_APPROVAL` → run `@02-architect`
   - After Gate 2 → `PENDING_SPRINT_APPROVAL` → run `@03-manager`
   - After Gate 3 → `IMPLEMENTATION` → run `@04-dev-fullstack`
3. Continue only after the file is updated.

### Maintenance track
1. Check off the maintenance gate matching the current maintenance `STATUS`.
2. Update maintenance `STATUS`:
   - After Gate M1 → `PENDING_MAINTENANCE_SPRINT_APPROVAL` → run `@03-manager` (and `@02-architect` if structural impact is flagged)
   - After Gate M2 → `MAINTENANCE_IMPLEMENTATION` → run `@04-dev-fullstack` / `@07-dev-maintenance`
3. Continue only after the file is updated.

## GitHub & merge phrases

Gates 1–4 and M1–M3 remain product/process approvals in `docs/PROJECT_STATE.md`. GitHub merges are a **separate phrase layer**. Gate 3 is Sprint Tickets approval — it is **not** the staging merge gate.

### Branch standards
- `main`: production (protected; merge only via PR after `DEPLOY TO PRODUCTION`).
- `staging`: integration / staging environment (merge only via PR after `MERGE TO STAGING` or human GitHub merge).
- `feature/*` or `fix/*`: ephemeral ticket branches from `docs/TASKS.md` (e.g. `feature/ticket-12-refactor-auth`).
- Never commit directly to `main` or `staging`. Never force-push to `main` or `staging`.

### Ticket → staging → production (shared by build and maintenance)
1. `@04-dev-fullstack` or `@07-dev-maintenance` branches from `staging`, implements, opens a Draft PR targeting `staging`.
2. On UI-touching tickets, `@08-ui-artist` captures screenshots, reads the images, and notes `visual OK` or `[!]`.
3. `@06-dev-qa` verifies on the PR (local + CI); marks ticket `[x]` or `[!]`. Do not `[x]` while visual review is `[!]`.
4. On `[x]`, PR is marked ready; user replies `MERGE TO STAGING` (or merges in GitHub).
5. After merge, `@06-dev-qa` may smoke against the staging backend / environment and CI build artifacts.
6. `@05-dev-ops` opens PR `staging` → `main` when the release set is ready; user replies `DEPLOY TO PRODUCTION`.

### On user reply `MERGE TO STAGING`
1. Confirm the named feature/fix PR targets `staging`, CI is green, and the ticket is `[x]` (or explicitly waived).
2. Allow merge of that PR into `staging` (agent may merge only after this phrase, or confirm the user already merged in GitHub).
3. Do **not** check off Gate 4 / M3. Hand off to `@06-dev-qa` for staging smoke when applicable.

### On user reply `DEPLOY TO PRODUCTION`
1. Check off Gate 4 (build) or Gate M3 (maintenance) as appropriate.
2. Set build `STATUS: PRODUCTION_RELEASE` or maintenance `STATUS: MAINTENANCE_RELEASED`.
3. Allow `@05-dev-ops` to merge the `staging` → `main` release PR and provision / ship. Never deploy or merge to `main` without this exact phrase.

## Ticket status scheme (docs/TASKS.md)
- `[ ]` todo
- `[~]` implemented, awaiting visual + QA
- `[x]` QA_PASSED
- `[!]` blocked / bugs noted on the ticket

## Agent references
Use filenames only: `@01-researcher`, `@02-architect`, `@03-manager`, `@04-dev-fullstack`, `@05-dev-ops`, `@06-dev-qa`, `@07-dev-maintenance`, `@08-ui-artist`.
